msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:12
#: 7e37166980a64470854ca77040818ed0
msgid ""
"A **graph** is a fundamental mathematical structure consisting of "
"vertices (or nodes) connected by edges. Graphs model relationships and "
"connections in countless real-world systems, from social networks to "
"transportation systems, making them one of the most versatile data "
"structures in computer science."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:39
#: d29425eca37f4305adb7ff8dea24c680
msgid ""
"Graphs are ubiquitous in computer science and beyond. Understanding graph"
" theory is essential for solving problems in networking, optimization, "
"data analysis, and artificial intelligence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:44
#: 636c0262087f4e8db877df40288296f2
msgid "Mathematical Model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:47
#: 1425f9a78b474e219ad6d64a82ab8e85
msgid "Formal Definition"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:50
#: 5ee6c1d7d0b84aa6a58e4d1809e11541
msgid "Graph Definition"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:52
#: f674659bd01d4a48b2ab1ba85c70d471
msgid "A graph :math:`G` is defined as an ordered pair:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:54
#: 208c8573553d42e29479def3570608f1
msgid "G = (V, E)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:58
#: 56b2acaba71a4cf49d75ec6ca2c947f1
msgid "where:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:59
#: ffcac37bdbeb4e30936b5fb63b489506
msgid ":math:`V` is a **set of vertices** (or nodes)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:60
#: c03abe5be59e4ce8b45dfbdb63100aa1
msgid ":math:`E` is a **set of edges** connecting pairs of vertices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:62
#: 4611cef6bf624d6a98170b5ab31345ab
msgid "For undirected graphs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:64
#: 5879b4bd7dd2421cb625edf3fc39e8a8
msgid "E \\subseteq \\{\\{u, v\\} : u, v \\in V, u \\neq v\\}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:68
#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:117
#: d388b71159d54b5fac274f967f95b2e9 d70a35205cf4466e9169ab711d845d65
msgid "For directed graphs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:70
#: 934821201d034858976a145eddb47e0c
#, python-brace-format
msgid "E \\subseteq \\{(u, v) : u, v \\in V, u \\neq v\\}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:74
#: 7f13913ca8bb46d1b8f296420cb3509d
msgid ""
"**Example**: :math:`G = (\\{A, B, C\\}, \\{\\{A,B\\}, \\{B,C\\}, "
"\\{A,C\\}\\})`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:77
#: c04920e537254fbf9b0f6ac6ab6b06f9
msgid "Special Graph Types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:79
#: 23daf9841e4647e2bbda1795e4136109
msgid "**Simple Graph**: No self-loops, no multiple edges"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:81
#: 8c4c1fcf35194d1ba64af0950efb160f
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\forall e \\in E: e = \\{u, v\\} \\text{ where } u \\neq v"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:85
#: 126ad7b48c6a4784854903e872b31792
msgid "**Multigraph**: Allows multiple edges between same vertices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:87
#: db05427a2d14483eafc605bc88f380a9
#, python-brace-format
msgid "E \\text{ is a multiset}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:91
#: 83cc8113c598401b9c5261bb7cb45a9d
msgid "**Complete Graph** :math:`K_n`: All vertices connected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:93
#: 711196090ee54fc1814dac975d85a8e4
#, python-brace-format
msgid "|E| = \\binom{n}{2} = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:98
#: 6eac4930da86456a91900dd4a58c053e
msgid "Graph Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:101
#: bfdcd8d068034b18b43550e681c722f7
msgid "Degree"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:103
#: c28ec3e1bba4400582a3d96e3e4e5c43
msgid ""
"The **degree** of a vertex :math:`v` is the number of edges incident to "
"it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:105
#: 280fdd288fd244bba3bcb5a05fb34683
#, python-brace-format
msgid "deg(v) = |\\{e \\in E : v \\in e\\}|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:109
#: cac9ae66efad4dd98e3b023156c09432
msgid "**Handshaking Lemma**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:111
#: 5a40dffe2aad4ac9b0a48acf29a3921b
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\sum_{v \\in V} deg(v) = 2|E|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:115
#: 53586333f43642898d552f2b7d1a0bcf
msgid "This states that the sum of all degrees equals twice the number of edges."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:119
#: 5a32450ab300427eafd157e5e24b5a79
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"deg^{in}(v) &= |\\{(u, v) \\in E\\}| \\quad \\text{(in-degree)} \\\\\n"
"deg^{out}(v) &= |\\{(v, u) \\in E\\}| \\quad \\text{(out-degree)} \\\\\n"
"deg(v) &= deg^{in}(v) + deg^{out}(v)\n"
"\\end{aligned}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:128
#: b2ae6d601a0b4cfca96efc44c8a303b0
msgid "Paths and Connectivity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:130
#: 360214993efa4190bfa94911dbba2ce6
msgid "A **path** from :math:`u` to :math:`v` is a sequence of vertices:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:132
#: 66c15e64db5d475eaa4f8e76a51149da
msgid ""
"P = (v_0, v_1, \\ldots, v_k) \\text{ where } v_0 = u, v_k = v, \\text{ "
"and } \\{v_i, v_{i+1}\\} \\in E"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:136
#: a844b8d25d0c445a996f9ee64fc9f262
msgid "**Path length**: Number of edges in the path (:math:`k`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:138
#: af1bb2adb58f4d2999f940da7ecf56db
msgid ""
"A graph is **connected** if there exists a path between every pair of "
"vertices:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:140
#: 0d48349854214af1ac1fa2f9984df8a6
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\forall u, v \\in V: \\exists \\text{ path from } u \\text{ to } v"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:144
#: bc5a41cf8ed24b82a0a4d31535a9f4dc
msgid "**Distance** between vertices :math:`u` and :math:`v`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:146
#: 6c6413faf69a46948ad6eebf0df1ca3e
#, python-brace-format
msgid "d(u, v) = \\min\\{|P| : P \\text{ is a path from } u \\text{ to } v\\}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:151
#: 3d4cbf6ec6b24b28a58d59c6aff6a7df
msgid "Cycles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:153
#: fe389d34f5bb48ad9c0e82db3f6ce6df
msgid "A **cycle** is a path where :math:`v_0 = v_k` and :math:`k \\geq 3`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:155
#: f0cb922ab74446dcb5169d35d39b6afd
#, python-brace-format
msgid "C = (v_0, v_1, \\ldots, v_k) \\text{ where } v_0 = v_k"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:159
#: 468ce5d8f97d40be8d442cf97bd5f6c0
msgid "A graph is **acyclic** if it contains no cycles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:161
#: 073d8ed3cecc40699fe6b89f17bef543
msgid ""
"For directed graphs, a **Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG)** has no directed "
"cycles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:164
#: a5227fb553ec477588edcede80c40715
msgid "Subgraphs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:166
#: c50a339341a84d5da09ae09b8442d5d8
msgid ":math:`G' = (V', E')` is a **subgraph** of :math:`G = (V, E)` if:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:168
#: b7665525fb204a09a3067194d5deed59
#, python-brace-format
msgid "V' \\subseteq V \\text{ and } E' \\subseteq E"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:172
#: 368bebd1c6ae4912b788645eb639fbac
msgid "**Induced subgraph** on :math:`V' \\subseteq V`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/graph_structures/general.rst:174
#: 1e542a3fecb642f287368bf27ab03ed0
#, python-brace-format
msgid "G[V'] = (V', E') \\text{ where } E' = \\{e \\in E : e \\subseteq V'\\}"
msgstr ""

